{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep the Sabbath.</b> He returned to it again on account of 'those who profane it.' <b>Those who profane it.</b> In the open — shall be put to death. For anyone who performs labor on it in secret — <b>shall be cut off</b> by Heaven, since the matter is not known to the court so that it can execute judgment upon him. <b>Anyone who performs labor on it</b> etc. We have heard the punishment; from where the warning? Scripture says: 'and the seventh day' etc. I have only the punishment for daytime labor; from where the punishment for nighttime labor? Scripture says: 'מחלליה מות יומת.' We have heard the punishment for nighttime labor; from where the warning for the day? Scripture says: 'ויום השביעי שבת.' What does Scripture say 'שבת' for? To include the night within the warning."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:23.119536073Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}